<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fretilin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1974–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Revolutionary Front for an Independent East Timor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fretilin, the Revolutionary Front for an Independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a>, was founded in 1974 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution">Carnation Revolution</a> in Portugal. It won a brief civil war in 1975 and declared independence on 28 November, nine days before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> invaded. Its armed wing, Falintil, led the resistance through the occupation, and Fretilin became one of the leading parties of independent East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fretilin.jpg" alt="Fretilin" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_FRETILIN_(East_Timor).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
